# Docker build context for the web image (compose builds it with `context: ./apps/web`).
#
# The Dockerfile copies an explicit path list, so none of this is needed for correctness; it is
# needed because the daemon tars and sends the whole context before the first RUN, and
# `apps/web` holds two directories that make that absurd: `node_modules` (~400 MB) and `.next`
# (a build produced by whatever host last ran it). Sending the latter is worse than slow — a
# `.next` built on the host would be a bundle whose platform, environment variables and
# `OXBOW_API_ORIGIN` were decided outside the image, and the image would then claim a build it
# did not perform.

node_modules/
.next/
out/
.turbo/
.test-output/
playwright-report/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
src/**/*.test.ts
src/**/*.test.tsx
tests/
scripts/
CONTRACT-GAPS.md
Dockerfile
